# cargo mutants on one file, on the cluster. Needs cargo-mutants in ~/.cargo/bin
# (docs/HPC_OFFLOAD.md). Job 20898 (16 CPUs) ran an earlier form of this plan, with the lists
# in $TMPDIR and a trailing echo: 42 mutants in 6 minutes. This exact form has not run yet.
# Submit: scripts/hpc/hpc-submit --cpus 16 --mem 16G --time 0:30:00 --label "mutants probe" scripts/hpc/plans/mutants-probe.plan
#
# `any`: cargo mutants exits 2 when a mutant is missed, which reads recorded(exit 2), and
# hpc-fetch notes it. Any other failure (a red baseline, a usage error) also reads
# recorded(exit N), so the last step is a `pass` check that at least one mutant was tested.
# The lists (caught.txt, missed.txt, ...) come back under out/mutants.out/.
# EXPECT  NAME             COMMAND
any       mutants-version  cargo mutants --version
any       mutants-net      cargo mutants -p konnect-sexp --file crates/konnect-sexp/src/net.rs --jobs 4 --timeout 120 --output "$RUN_OUT"
pass      mutants-ran      cd "$RUN_OUT/mutants.out" && cat caught.txt missed.txt timeout.txt unviable.txt | grep -q .
